# Self-managed Docker image with AWS secret custody (Track C of ./README.md):
# the published image on your own host, using AWS only for secrets (Secrets
# Manager + KMS). Copy to `.env.aws-no-ecs` (gitignored) and run from this
# directory:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.aws-no-ecs -f docker-compose.aws-no-ecs.yml up -d
#
# The bundled Postgres exists so the stack runs standalone; production points
# DATABASE_URL at your own TLS-verified Postgres (README, Track B step 3) and
# starts only the server with `--no-deps server`.
#
# The AWS ECS track is ./.env.aws-ecs.example; the no-AWS track is ./.env.example.
# Full server config reference: ../../CONFIGURATION.md

# Required: pin an explicit published release LATER THAN v0.17.0. This stack
# relies on server features v0.17.0 lacks (ack-keygen in the image, the
# storage-encryption key file, GUARDIAN_ALLOWED_ACCOUNT_SCHEMES, prod-stage
# defaults); an older image boots anyway and silently stores PLAINTEXT. Left
# blank on purpose: Compose refuses to start until you set it. Guardian 0.17.x
# runs on Miden 0.16 (../../MIDEN_COMPATIBILITY.md). Never run `latest`.
GUARDIAN_VERSION=

# Required: Miden network the server targets (MidenTestnet | MidenDevnet |
# MidenLocal). The server refuses to start when unset or unrecognized.
GUARDIAN_NETWORK_TYPE=MidenTestnet

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Production: your own Postgres over verified TLS (mount the CA bundle, see the
# commented volume in docker-compose.aws-no-ecs.yml):
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@db.example.com:5432/guardian?sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=/etc/guardian/tls/ca.pem
#
# Evaluation: the bundled Postgres (no backups, no TLS). The two values must
# agree: POSTGRES_PASSWORD initializes the bundled database on first run,
# DATABASE_URL is what the server dials. URL-safe characters only. The compose
# file does not interpolate DATABASE_URL (or any other server variable), so this
# line is the single source and an exported shell variable cannot override it.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
DATABASE_URL=postgres://guardian:change-me@postgres:5432/guardian

# --- AWS --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: region holding the Secrets Manager secrets and the KMS key.
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# Credentials for the container. This file is the container's env_file, so
# static keys go here (uncomment) and nowhere else; nothing is read from your
# shell. A long-lived host should instead leave these commented and rely on an
# instance/container role through the SDK's default credential chain. The
# principal needs secretsmanager:GetSecretValue on the secrets below and
# kms:GetPublicKey + kms:Sign on the key.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# Required: Secrets Manager name/ARN of the Falcon ACK key. Created by
#   ./scripts/aws-deploy.sh bootstrap-ack-keys   (with the KMS ARN exported)
# The bootstrap commands name secrets <STACK_NAME>/server/...; use YOUR stack name.
GUARDIAN_ACK_FALCON_SECRET_ID=<your-stack>/server/ack-falcon-secret-key

# Required: KMS key id/ARN/alias for the ECDSA ACK signer (ECC_SECG_P256K1 /
# SIGN_VERIFY). Created by ./scripts/aws-deploy.sh bootstrap-kms-ecdsa-key
GUARDIAN_ACK_ECDSA_KMS_KEY_ID=alias/<your-stack>-ack-ecdsa

# Recommended: Secrets Manager name/ARN of the storage-encryption key document
# ({active, keys}). Created by ./scripts/aws-deploy.sh bootstrap-storage-encryption-key
# Presence turns encryption on; enable against an EMPTY store only. Comment out
# to run with plaintext payloads.
GUARDIAN_STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SECRET_ID=<your-stack>/server/storage-encryption-key

# Optional: dashboard operator allowlist secret (Secrets Manager name/ARN,
# object entries for explicit permissions). Hot-reloaded.
# GUARDIAN_OPERATOR_PUBLIC_KEYS_SECRET_ID=<your-stack>/server/operators

# --- Dashboard ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: 32-byte hex (64 chars) for pagination cursors; pin one value and
# reuse it on every replica: openssl rand -hex 32
GUARDIAN_DASHBOARD_CURSOR_SECRET=replace-with-64-hex-chars

# --- Account signature scheme ---------------------------------------------------
# Schemes NEW accounts may register with (falcon, ecdsa). Recommended: ecdsa,
# the scheme with hosted-signer (KMS) support; Falcon is second-class. Applies
# to new registrations only: existing accounts keep their scheme for life, and
# both ACK keys are still required. Unset or blank allows both.
GUARDIAN_ALLOWED_ACCOUNT_SCHEMES=ecdsa

# --- Browser clients ----------------------------------------------------------
# Required for production browser clients: exact origins, comma-separated
# (wildcards rejected). Unset -> permissive Any origin, credentials disabled.
GUARDIAN_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://accounts.example.com

# --- Metrics (Prometheus) ------------------------------------------------------
# Published on 127.0.0.1:9464 only; gate scrapes with the bearer token.
GUARDIAN_METRICS_ENABLED=true
GUARDIAN_METRICS_BEARER_TOKEN=change-me

# --- Replicas ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Must equal the number of server replicas sharing this database (README.md,
# Track B step 7). Each replica enforces global / GUARDIAN_MAX_REPLICAS.
GUARDIAN_MAX_REPLICAS=1

# --- Production defaults (applied by GUARDIAN_ENV=prod, override to tune) -------
# With GUARDIAN_ENV=prod the server starts with the production profile: 200
# req/s burst per IP and endpoint, 5000 req/min per IP across HTTP and gRPC,
# 32 connections per pool (two pools per replica), 50 concurrent accounts per
# canonicalization pass, JSON logs. Set a variable only to change it.
# GUARDIAN_RATE_BURST_PER_SEC=200
# GUARDIAN_RATE_PER_MIN=5000
# GUARDIAN_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE=32
# GUARDIAN_METADATA_DB_POOL_MAX_SIZE=32
# GUARDIAN_CANONICALIZATION_MAX_CONCURRENT_ACCOUNTS=50
# GUARDIAN_LOG_FORMAT=json

# --- Optional tuning -----------------------------------------------------------
# Same knobs as ./.env.example.
# GUARDIAN_BIND_ADDR=127.0.0.1
# GUARDIAN_HTTP_PORT=3000
# GUARDIAN_GRPC_PORT=50051
# GUARDIAN_METRICS_PORT=9464
# GUARDIAN_MIDEN_RPC_ENDPOINT=https://rpc.example.com
